{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1209 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "8639ab920f7069909ece69296b163f26553edb821917c23f61a78929ff343f41" :edb/db-before-t 1208 :edb/db-after-t 1209 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534521 50 #inst "2026-10-12T01:48:47.993Z" 13194139534521 17592186045417 true] [17592186118496 1078 #edb/ref 17592186118500 13194139534521 17592186045417 true] [17592186119811 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424110 13194139534521 17592186045417 true] [17592186120397 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534521 17592186045417 true] [17592186120397 1071 "Consider the matrix given by $A = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 8 \\\\ -2 & -11 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$. Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b = \\begin{bmatrix}14 \\\\ -15 \\\\ k + 5\\end{bmatrix}$ belongs to $Col(A)$." 13194139534521 17592186045417 false] [17592186120397 1071 "Consider the matrix given by $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 8 \\\\ -2 & -11 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ -15 \\\\ k+5\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(A).$" 13194139534521 17592186045417 true] [17592186120397 1074 "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ then the equation $Ax=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 8 & 14 \\\\ -2 & -11 & -15 \\\\ 1 & 6 & k+5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & k+5 \\\\ -2 & -11 & -15 \\\\ 3 & 8 & 14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & k+5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2k-5 \\\\ 3 & 8 & 14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & k+5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2k-5 \\\\ 0 & -10 & -3k-1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+10{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & k+5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2k-5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 17k-51\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=k+5 \\\\ {x}_{2}=2k-5 \\\\ 0=17k-51.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=17k-51,$ which means that $k=3.$" 13194139534521 17592186045417 true] [17592186120515 1074 "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(E),$ we need to check if the equation $Ex=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[E\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[E\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -16 & 28 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ \\text{ }0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}+7{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}=2 \\\\ 0=-1 \\\\ {x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}-{x}_{4}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get a false statement $0=-1.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(E).$" 13194139534521 17592186045417 true] [17592186120515 1074 "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(E),$ we need to check if the equation $Ex=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[E\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[E\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -16 & 28 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ \\text{ }0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}+7{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}=2 \\\\ 0=-1 \\\\ {x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}-{x}_{4}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get a false statement $0=-1.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(E).$" 13194139534521 17592186045417 false] [17592186247190 1074 "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ then the equation $Ax=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ -5 & 1 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ 0 & 6 & 42\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ 0 & 0 & 42+2k\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=10 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}=k \\\\ 0=42+2k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=42+2k,$ which means that $k=-21.$" 13194139534521 17592186045417 true] [17592186247190 1074 "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ then the equation $Ax=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ -5 & 1 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ 0 & 6 & 42\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ 0 & 0 & 42+2k\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=10 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}=k \\\\ 0=42+2k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=42+2k,$ which means that $k=-21.$" 13194139534521 17592186045417 false] [17592186317416 1074 "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(E),$ we need to check if the equation $Ex=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[E\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[E\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 16 & -4 & 10 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}8{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}=4 \\\\ 0=-9 \\\\ 11{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}-{x}_{4}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get a false statement $0=-9.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(E).$" 13194139534521 17592186045417 true] [17592186317416 1074 "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(E),$ we need to check if the equation $Ex=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[E\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[E\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 16 & -4 & 10 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}8{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}=4 \\\\ 0=-9 \\\\ 11{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}-{x}_{4}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get a false statement $0=-9.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(E).$" 13194139534521 17592186045417 false] [17592186424103 1043 #edb/ref 17592186424111 13194139534521 17592186045417 true] [17592186424103 1043 #edb/ref 17592186424112 13194139534521 17592186045417 true] [17592186424103 1043 #edb/ref 17592186424113 13194139534521 17592186045417 true] [17592186424103 1043 #edb/ref 17592186424114 13194139534521 17592186045417 true] [17592186424103 1043 #edb/ref 17592186424115 13194139534521 17592186045417 true] [17592186424103 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534521 17592186045417 true] [17592186424103 1045 "The Column Space of a Matrix" 13194139534521 175921860454